WEBVTT

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.030
<b>Skull-face Bookseller Honda-san</b>

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:06.510
<b>A Book about Life, Death, and Rebirth</b>

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:06.140
Hi, pardon me...

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:07.130
Yes?

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:12.190
Do you have the volume of <i>Yokohama 
*** SF</i> that came out last week?

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.910
Sure, let me check.

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:16.490
Thank you.

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:19.920
I really can't find it anywhere,

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.910
even though it just came out.

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:26.030
<b>Search</b>

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.030
<i>I never knew it was so popular.</i>

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:26.030
<b>Yokohama</b>

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:28.650
<i>I've been curious about it 
ever since I saw it online.</i>

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.600
<i>Maybe I'll buy it later.</i>

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:32.670
<b>Local stock</b>

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:32.670
<b>Sold out</b>

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.380
<i>Oh, too bad.</i>

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.450
<i>Let's see if I can put in an order.</i>

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.040
<b>Stock at other stores</b>

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.040
<b>All gone</b>

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.310
<b>Wholesaler stock</b>

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.310
<b>Not responding</b>

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:39.710
<b>Publisher stock</b>

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:39.710
<b>Empty</b>

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:41.710
<b>S.O.L.</b>

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:42.710
You don't have it, do you?

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:45.700
S-Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:50.710
Unfortunately, we're out of stock, 
and we aren't able to order more.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:51.850
I see.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:54.030
I understand.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.140
I'm so sorry!

00:01:56.890 --> 00:02:00.270
Excuse me, do you have <i>Yokohama *** SF</i>?

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:01.960
It came out around last week.

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:04.100
I'm sorry, we're out of stock.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:06.630
Not here, too!

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:08.640
Do you have <i>Yokohama *** S</i>F?

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:09.730
We don't.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:11.840
<b>Heeunngh...</b>

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:11.980
Hi, do you have <i>Yokohama *** S</i>—

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:13.150
No, we don't.

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:15.080
<b>Nooo!</b>

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:17.600
<i>This is the first time everyone's 
asked for the same book.</i>

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:21.220
<i>To think we'd have sold out of
 all copies on the first day...</i>

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:23.980
<b>Careless mistake</b>

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:23.590
<i>I haven't bought one for myself, either!</i>

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:28.090
<b>Staff only</b>

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:27.840
Man, that book sold like crazy.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:31.000
I did make a follow-up order.

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:34.330
<b>In charge of novels and light novels</b>

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.330
It's popular, so I'm sure it'll get a reprint,

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:38.700
but Kadokawa's relatively slow about those, 
so who knows when we'll get them.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.320
Right...

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:42.640
Too many manga!

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:43.970
There's nowhere to put them!

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:46.430
There's no place for the new books shelf.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.350
Help me, Fullface!

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:50.650
Let me use your shelves!

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:53.890
Our section isn't much better.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:55.150
I don't think I can.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:57.850
I just walked in on something terrifying.

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:01.190
I can make it!

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:02.270
I can make the train!

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:03.610
If I haul ass,

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:04.430
I can totally make it!

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:05.340
Shit, yeah, I can—

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:05.890
Nope!

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:09.740
Look, he's been prepping too many shelves 
for new books. He's lost his mind.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:11.260
By prepping too much?!

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:11.870
I'm tired.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:12.530
I'm dying.

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:13.910
Hey, can I hug you a little?

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:17.390
I feel like I can sprint to the station 
if I get re-energized with a hug.

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:18.090
Pretty please?

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.470
Just for a second.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:20.580
Hey, our shift's over.

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:21.670
God damn!

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:24.770
Later, guys!

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:26.510
<b>Kami-chan clocks out!!</b>

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:31.500
Is it just me, or are new books 
not selling as well lately?

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.870
We just end up returning
 them after a month, right?

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:35.960
Since we don't wanna 
stock crap we don't need.

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:41.690
But as soon we make the return, we get a ton 
of sales, and we have to order in a hurry.

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:42.900
We know how that feels.

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:47.460
And don't you think the turnover is 
insanely fast on the new books shelves?

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:54.570
<b>New books</b>

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.620
It's practically a tile puzzle.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:53.770
Seriously, I can't keep doing 
this every single month.

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:56.910
I told you, too many manga 
is being published!

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:59.620
I'm getting caught in the crossfire here!

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:59.840
<b>Bookseller/manga author</b>

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:02.610
<i>Having too much stock presents a problem,</i>

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:07.590
<i>so booksellers tend to get touchier 
than usual about new releases.</i>

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:11.330
No, that's <i>absolutely not</i> gonna sell!

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:15.210
The author's an unknown newbie, aren't they?

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:17.330
It's your job to push them
 harder as their publisher.

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:20.560
And it doesn't look like there's 
any hype online, either.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.250
No, we can't just add more stock!

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:27.870
Was that from a publisher?

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.130
Yeah.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:35.450
It's just not that easy to sell a book 
that's had no previews or hype online.

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:38.080
We can't just add more stock, huh?

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:42.390
Unlike famous works, they won't
sell without any effort.

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:43.790
Of course.

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:47.530
But it'd be a different story if the 
publisher were to push it aggressively.

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:51.180
I'd be like, "Sure, we'll make 
the effort to sell them!"

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:54.880
<i>She's so nice.</i>

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:56.630
<i>I'm so moved.</i>

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:01.210
Speaking of which, Honda, you've 
been doing that all day today.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:02.700
Are you done checking the flops?

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:04.410
I'm still not done!

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:11.880
<b>stock</b>

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:11.880
<b>There's nothing here!</b>

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:11.880
<b>Lies!</b>

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:07.030
<i>Every book is a new book at first.</i>

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:07.820
There's nothing here!

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:11.220
<i>But after that period, it doesn't sell as well.</i>

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:09.120
Lies!

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:14.920
<i>These books are called "deathbed books".</i>

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:14.950
Dammit, <i>Skull-face Bookseller</i> isn't selling!

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:15.030
<b>Dammit, <i>Skull-face Bookseller</i> 
isn't selling!</b>

00:05:13.510 --> 00:05:21.090
<b>Deathbed books</b>

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:17.250
<b>Bye!</b>

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:17.250
<b>Bookstore</b>

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:21.090
<b>Wholesaler</b>

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:21.090
<b>Publisher</b>

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:18.510
<i>They get returned to the publisher 
through the wholesaler.</i>

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:16.160
Bye!

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:19.630
I'm back.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:24.390
<b>Foreign Comics</b>

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:24.390
<i>Okay then, let's get started.</i>

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:28.380
<i>Shove the books that won't fit 
onto the lower shelves.</i>

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:33.160
It hurts!

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:36.340
<b>* Hallucination</b>

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:36.080
Stick me in more gently!

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:38.700
No!

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:42.210
I can't! My wrapping is coming apart!

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:43.390
<i>Shut up and get in!</i>

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:47.210
No! Stop! No!

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:53.590
Don't forget...

00:05:53.590 --> 00:06:02.950
<b>* Hallucination</b>

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:56.450
You shouldn't be so forceful.

00:05:56.450 --> 00:05:59.600
Deathbed books get sent back

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:02.960
because they don't fit on the shelves.

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:04.820
You're right.

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:07.100
Who the hell are you talking to?

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:13.510
<i>I finally managed to figure 
out the upper shelves.</i>

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:16.270
Koomote-san?!

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:21.510
<b>List</b>

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:21.510
I have to return our deathbed books too,

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:25.770
but the books in my section move so slowly.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:32.690
She's the type who speaks 
differently when emotional

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:27.950
If we keep returning books at this rate,

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:30.890
the whole publisher is going to go down.

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:40.830
Will you choose this shelf, empty from having 
had entire publishers' worth of books returned?

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:45.450
Or this shelf, jam packed 
because you kept everything?

00:06:45.450 --> 00:06:47.440
Section Chief Pestmask!

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:48.830
Just kidding.

00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:51.970
Don't let it get to you too much.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:54.850
The deathbed books are just a rough guide.

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:56.930
You can try returning them,

00:06:56.930 --> 00:07:00.820
and then re-stock them if we get inquiries.

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:02.950
You're right.

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:07.060
The reality is that if it isn't selling, 
we aren't getting inquiries, either.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:09.920
I have to say goodbye.

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:11.330
Yep, go for it!

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:12.920
The difference in passion...

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:16.910
<i>It must be hard for Koomote-san.</i>

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:20.370
<i>There's no telling when her 
books will start selling again.</i>

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:24.540
<i>Here we go!</i>

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:28.650
<b>Poor Seller
 Volume 2</b>

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:28.260
<i>A series with only some 
volumes on their deathbed!</i>

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:30.510
<b>Not selling</b>

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:30.510
<b>Not selling</b>

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:33.920
<b>Selling</b>

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:33.920
<b>Selling</b>

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:30.680
<i>I see, this is tough.</i>

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:33.920
<i>If we return these, some books in 
the series are going to be missing.</i>

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:36.250
<i>I wonder if I should not return them.</i>

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:47.300
<b>Poor Seller
Volume 2</b>

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:47.300
<b>Poor Seller
 Volume 4</b>

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:40.400
<i>Ah, what do I do?!</i>

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:43.290
<i>It's a middle volume 
and a final volume!</i>

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:47.300
<i>It'll look absolutely awful if 
we sell only the other ones!</i>

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:51.040
<i>I wonder if someone will 
suddenly buy this book.</i>

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:54.680
<i>The books that are selling 
won't fit on the shelves.</i>

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:59.310
<i>I have to return the deathbed books, or 
I'll take those non-consenting books and...</i>

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:01.680
No!

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:04.950
<b>Poor Seller
 Volume 2</b>

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:07.650
<i>It's okay...</i>

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:11.890
<i>I'm just returning some other deathbed 
books to free up some space.</i>

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:15.550
<i>That'll at least get me out 
of this tightly-packed problem.</i>

00:08:15.790 --> 00:08:17.190
<b>Delay the inevitable!!</b>

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:23.900
<b>Book</b>

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:23.900
<b>Book</b>

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:23.560
<i>All that "deathbed" really means is that 
they aren't selling at this particular store.</i>

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:29.800
<b>Out-of-print</b>

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:29.680
<i>These days, even out-of-print 
books often rise from the dead.</i>

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:34.440
<b>That's me, isn't it?!</b>

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:34.440
<b>Revived book</b>

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:34.010
<i>Such timeless books are 
called "revived books."</i>

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:37.810
<i>A non-fiction book on the deadly ebola virus</i>

00:08:37.810 --> 00:08:44.250
<i>became a top-seller when it 
was released twenty years ago.</i>

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:51.630
Not found

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:51.190
<i>Eventually that book fell on its deathbed, 
and was out of print for a long time.</i>

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:58.020
<i>But with the 2014 ebola outbreak in 
West Africa, it was quickly revived.</i>

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:01.800
<i>It traveled through time to be 
resuscitated as a new edition.</i>

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:07.550
<i>That book further opened the floodgates to 
a myriad of books on contagious diseases,</i>

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:10.380
<i>and we even saw in-depth 
special sections emerge.</i>

00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:18.180
Contagious Diseases in Your Lives

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:17.090
<i>I never would have thought books 
come back to life like this.</i>

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:20.650
I remember that.

00:09:20.650 --> 00:09:23.790
It's not something you see 
a lot of in the comics section.

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:27.440
I guess some nostalgic favorites 
get revived sometimes.

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:30.300
Even that's a rare occurrence, though.

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:36.540
There was a book that a customer 
asked about, and it was out of print.

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:39.790
I'm sorry, this book is out of print.

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:41.740
We do seem to have an e-book.

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:47.450
<b>Customer</b>

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:44.120
I said I want a <i>book</i>!

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:47.450
You think I'd come all the way to 
a bookstore just to buy a damn <i>e-book</i>?!

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:47.450
I'm sorry!

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:52.800
I've found there's a high chance that 
I'll get yelled at for mentioning e-books,

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:55.450
so I decided to never bring them up again.

00:09:56.230 --> 00:09:58.100
I should be careful, too.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:00.500
Honda-san.

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:03.940
I bought the reprints.

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:07.870
That's the book I missed, too!

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:09.930
<i>Yokohama *** SF</i>!

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:11.990
Congratulations.

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:15.010
Come on, you said you missed 
your chance to buy it, too.

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:16.760
I kept a copy.

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:20.110
Th-Th-Th...

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:20.110
<b>Thank you so much!!</b>

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:23.710
<i>Life, death, and rebirth.</i>

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:30.990
Hi, new book here

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:30.990
Huh? I'm not
 selling well

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:30.990
Looks like this is it

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:30.990
Sent back... 
Deathbed...

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:30.990
Wait a sec, 
sudden demand!

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:30.990
Whoa, it's revived

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:30.990
<b>Book</b>

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:28.880
<i>I think daily about the eternal
 cycle of a book's rebirth.</i>
